# PENDING (WP-175): the input comp.lh.o is a reference's `ld -r` output passed through `objcopy --localize-hidden`; the lane has no step for either until WP-175's `partial` step lands. Then: build x1.o, `partial` it to comp.o (`ld -r x1.o -o comp.o`), `objcopy --localize-hidden comp.o comp.lh.o`, and rename this file to .test.
# The pre-link idiom (WP-154's cells prelink-lh-x-*; WP-176): a component
# made by `ld -r` and passed through `objcopy --localize-hidden` keeps
# its copies of the COMDAT groups DW.ref.__gxx_personality_v0 and
# DW.ref._ZTISt9exception, whose hidden weak symbols are now LOCAL. The
# component comes first, so its copies are kept (resolve.md §6.1) and
# x2.o's (and libstdc++.a members') copies dropped; x2.o's CIE
# personality pointer in .eh_frame and its .gcc_except_table type entry
# name the demoted weak hidden mentions, whose keys nothing live defines
# (the kept definitions are local). Those references are comdat-mismatch
# (§6.3 case (b)): the CIE and the LSDA are live. GNU ld and lld write 0
# into both and the first throw through x2.o's frames aborts
# ("terminate called after throwing an instance of 'std::runtime_error'",
# signal 6); mold refuses the .gcc_except_table reference.
#@ spec: resolve.md §6.3
#@ arch: aarch64 x86_64
#@ requires: g++

cxx -O1 x1.cc -o x1.o
cxx -O1 x2.cc -o x2.o
# partial ld -r x1.o -o comp.o                      (WP-175's step; syntax to come)
# objcopy --localize-hidden comp.o comp.lh.o        (the same package's tool step, or a fixture)

link(bfd,lld) g++ -static comp.lh.o x2.o -o prog
run(bfd,lld) prog
  exit: signal 6
link(mold,mortar) g++ -static comp.lh.o x2.o -o prog
  exit: fail
  diag(mold): DW.ref._ZTISt9exception refers to a discarded COMDAT section probably due to an ODR violation
  diag(mortar): symbol DW.ref.__gxx_personality_v0 is defined only in a discarded copy of COMDAT group DW.ref.__gxx_personality_v0
  diag(mortar): >>> referenced by x2.o:(.eh_frame+0x
  diag(mortar): symbol DW.ref._ZTISt9exception is defined only in a discarded copy of COMDAT group DW.ref._ZTISt9exception

link g++ -static x1.o x2.o -o direct
run direct
  exit: 11

#--- x1.cc
#include <stdexcept>
int f1(int x) {
  try {
    if (x) throw std::runtime_error("a");
  } catch (const std::exception &) {
    return 1;
  }
  return 0;
}
#--- x2.cc
#include <stdexcept>
int f2(int x) {
  if (x) throw std::runtime_error("b");
  return 0;
}
int f1(int);
int main(int argc, char **) {
  int r = f1(argc);
  try {
    f2(argc);
  } catch (const std::exception &) {
    r += 10;
  }
  return r;
}
